worry about writing down the code  though because after luna gives you your  dream address  it will also appear on your passport and  map now you can share that dream address  with anyone you wish  if you want to visit other islands the  process starts the same way talk to luna  but this time choose the  want to dream option from there you'll  input the dream address you'd like to  visit  note that there are some limitations  when you're visiting islands via a dream  address  you'll be free to explore the island  talk to villagers and this is the big  one here  download custom designs unfortunately  you won't be able to fish catch bugs  use the item shop or learn any diys  in addition to dream suite the august  update also brings a firework show every  sunday at 7 pm local time  i'm sure you'll also be delighted to  know that we can now back up  our islands finally it's a shame that  there have already been folks out there  lose their islands and  all their hard work due to save data  corruption or problems with their switch  that being said better late than never i  suppose and i'm thankful nintendo  finally added this to the game i would  suggest  all players do this first thing after  updating the game this one is actually  handled through the main menu before you  even enter your island it's a bit  confusing at first because the game kind  of leads you that maybe you shouldn't be  using it but that's simply referring to  the process of restoring your island  should something go wrong  definitely go ahead and choose the  option to enable the island backup  service  so that's it for the august update  fireworks dream suite and the island  backup service are all in new horizons  and while none of these updates are  completely mind-blowing  they're all welcome additions and i'm  happy to see nintendo keeping a steady  flow of content now for all the non-time  travelers out there we'll also see a few  new bugs and fish making their way to  the northern hemisphere this month both  the migratory locust  and rice grasshopper can be found on the  ground between the hours of 8 a.m  and 7 p.m you'll find the walker cicada  on trees between  8 a.m and 5 p.m the moray eel will be in  the sea  and available all day long the ray is  also in the sea but only  available from 4 am to 9 pm as for fresh  water the soft-shelled turtle can now be  found in rivers between the hours of 4  p.m  and 9 a.m there's also a new deep sea  creature to find and that's the flatworm  who you'll find between 4 pm  and 9 am as far as bugs and fish go for  the southern hemisphere  i'm sorry guys it's yet another sad  month because the tiger beetle is the  only new creature for you to catch  so which of these updates are you guys  most excited about let me know down in  the comments and consider giving a  thumbs up if you found this video  helpful  thanks so much for watching
 

